// RawSet::program_for). The matrices and registers come as the GE has them
// (core raw_blocks.rs, frame.rs RawTransform and RawCamera) and are applied
// one after the other, in the GE's order, as PPSSPP's vertex shaders do
// (VertexShaderGenerator.cpp: u_world, u_view, u_proj). raw_blocks.rs and
// raw_vertex.rs are the CPU's copy of this program: keep them in step. The
// outputs are those of nativeres_textured_v.cg (the same fragment programs).
//
// aPosition: the raw position (s8, s16 or float, as numbers), times
//   uFormat.x (the format's scale: 1/128, 1/32768, 1).
// aTexcoord: the raw texture coordinates (u8, u16 or float, as numbers);
//   uRawUv: scale u, v, offset u, v (raw_blocks::raw_uv: the format's scale
//   times TEXTURE_SCALE; scale 0 for formats without texture coordinates).
// aColorBytes: the two bytes of a 16-bit colour (5650, 5551, 4444), 0..255
//   each: reading the 16-bit field as one number came out wrong on the GPU
//   (measured on the Vita, 2026-11-08), bytes come out right.
// aColor32: an 8888 colour, 0..1 per channel.
// uFormat: x = the position scale, y = the colour format (VERTEX_TYPE bits
//   2..4): 0 none, 4 5650, 5 5551, 6 4444, 7 8888.
// aNormal: the raw normal (s8, s16 or float, as numbers; (byte 0..2) for
//   formats without one, unused then): only for lighting 3.
// aWeights0, aWeights1: the raw skinning weights 1-4 and 5-8 (u8, u16 or
//   float; read from byte 0 for formats with fewer, unused then: their bones
//   are zero). uSkin: x > 0.5 = skinned (frame.rs Draw::bones), y = what the
//   raw weights are multiplied by (1/128, 1/32768, 1). uBones: 8 bones of 3
//   rows (float4, as uploaded), zeros beyond the format's weights. Skinned
//   position = sum of weight x bone applied to (scaled x, y, z, 1)
//   (raw_blocks::model_space); normals with the bones' 3x3 parts.
// uWorld (3 rows), uView (3 rows), uProj (4 rows): the GE's matrices, row by
//   row (frame.rs RawTransform::world, RawCamera::view, ::projection).
// uFog: view z factor, FOG_END, FOG_SCALE: fog = (view z x .x + .y) x .z
//   (0, 1, 1 without fog: 1 = none).
// uViewport: origin x, y, scale x, y (RawCamera::viewport).
// uMaterial, uAmbient, uEmissive, uColors: frame.rs RawColors: colours as
//   whole numbers 0..255; uColors = (lighting, opaque, replace, doubled
//   alpha: blend factor "doubled source alpha", the vertex alpha doubled
//   instead, at most 255, after opaque and before replace).
// uScale: blend factor FIX A (frame.rs RawColors::scale): w > 0.5: last of
//   all, RGB = floor(RGB x uScale.rgb / 255) (blend.rs scale_color).
//   Lighting 3 (raw_vertex.rs lighting::LIGHTS): the vertex colour (white
//   without one) lit with directional lights (uLights, the light set, 22
//   float4, GpuLights) by its normal taken to world space with uWorld's 3x3
//   (turned around where uLights[21].w is 1, REVERSE_NORMAL), as
//   nativeres_3d_v.cg lights its GPU-lit vertices (GpuLights::color).
// wvp, uUvScale: as nativeres_3d_v.cg.
//
// Depth and the near plane: the GPU clips -w <= z <= w (measured). The PSP
// clips at its near plane z = -w and keeps everything beyond its far plane,
// so z goes out as (z - w) / 2: the GPU's near plane is the PSP's and its far
// plane is at z = 3w, out of reach. The viewport's z (set per camera by the
// display, sceGxmSetViewport) turns that into the depth the other draws
// write for the same PSP depth. No division by w here: a vertex behind the
// camera stays finite until the GPU clips its triangle.
//
// Compiled on the Vita with the shader compiler app (README.md "Shaders").
//
// Variants (generated from this file by scripts/shader-variants.sh: keep
// them in step), each for the draws that need no more, as PPSSPP makes its
// vertex shaders per bone count and lights. The full program costs every
// vertex its skinning and lighting code even when the uniforms switch them
// off (2026-11-10), and its size alone (uniforms, attributes) costs the GPU
// per draw (2026-11-17: MTX's riders, ~290 small draws, 5.5 ms less as
// plain programs).
// - RAW_PLAIN (nativeres_raw_plain_v.cg): no directional lights, one bone
//   (RAW_ONE_BONE, RAW_NO_LIGHTS). Nearly all draws but the riders.
// - RAW_PLAIN4 (nativeres_raw_plain4_v.cg): no directional lights, up to
//   four bones (RAW_FOUR_BONES, RAW_NO_LIGHTS).
// - RAW_LIT1 (nativeres_raw_lit1_v.cg): lights, one bone (RAW_ONE_BONE).
// - RAW_LIT4 (nativeres_raw_lit4_v.cg): lights, up to four bones
//   (RAW_FOUR_BONES: aWeights0 only, uBones[12]).
// - The lit variants (RAW_LIT1, RAW_LIT4 and their flat forms) take only
//   draws lit with directional lights (RAW_LIGHTS_ONLY, draw.rs
//   `raw_variant`): the unlit draws' colour rules are left out (52
//   instructions per vertex, 2026-11-18). The GPU runs a part switched by
//   a uniform whether it is on or not, so only the full program keeps both.
// - RAW_LIT1_FLAT, RAW_LIT4_FLAT (nativeres_raw_lit1flat_v.cg, _lit4flat_v):
//   as RAW_LIT1 / RAW_LIT4 for light sets whose specular coefficient is 0
//   or less and whose fourth light is all zeros (RAW_FLAT_LIGHTS, draw.rs
//   `flat_lights`). The GE's pow is 1 then (PspPow), so the powered
//   diffuse and the specular factor need no pow and no half vector, and the
//   fourth light, which adds exactly 0, is left out: the same sums, bit for
